# Runtime state produced by the scheduled reference-price refresh. The run log
# is operational history (Postgres holds the authoritative copy in a deployed
# environment) and the lock file is transient by definition - neither belongs
# in version control.
server/data/reference-prices/refresh-runs.json
server/data/reference-prices/.refresh.lock
tsconfig.next.tsbuildinfo

# NOTE: cashify-sessions/*.json and cashify-session.json are Playwright
# storageState files - they contain live Cashify session cookies. They are
# currently TRACKED in this repository (pre-existing), which is why they are
# not listed here: adding them now would leave them ignored-but-tracked, and
# untracking them would break any deploy that relies on the committed copy.
# See PRICING_REFERENCE_DATA_ARCHITECTURE.md ("Cashify session material") for
# the rotation/removal steps. CI does NOT use the committed files - it reads
# the CASHIFY_SESSION_STATE secret instead.

